      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Genus-level entry (starter row 58); cultivar sizes run from miniature to giant, so size is left unknown (NC State: 'Blue Mouse Ears' 8 in tall, 'Empress Wu' up to 50 in). Look-alikes: Aspidistra and Bergenia leaves (01g). Watering: RHS says containers need regular watering in summer, soil at least slightly damp, miniatures dislike wet roots in winter; NC State prefers moist, well-drained soil and warns against soggy soil in winter; no frequency, so interval 3 days is a guess. Light: RHS partial or light to medium shade (blue-leaved types light shade, yellow-leaved some sun); NC State morning sun and dappled shade, blue forms deeper shade; stored medium. Hardiness: RHS fully hardy, dies back in late autumn; NC State needs a dormant spell below 40 F and foliage dies back at 28 F; no temperature stored. Growth rate: only a model summary of the truncated NC State page says medium, so unknown (the fetch cut the NC State page; verbatim part covered watering, light, dormancy, pets). Habit rosette is a mapping of 'clumping herbaceous perennial'. Toxicity: ASPCA lists toxic to dogs and cats (saponins; vomiting, diarrhoea, depression), no severity word; NC State says all parts are toxic to cats, dogs and horses with no agent or signs. Severity 1 is our grading, depression mapped to lethargy. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
